# --- Source data downloads -------------------------------------------------
# Raw source files (Parquet from A2AJ, XML from Justice Laws) are not committed.
# They are large, they are not ours to redistribute, and the build is meant to
# be reproducible from the documented source URLs instead.
#
# The tax expenditure report snapshot is the exception - see
# docs/decisions.md, 2026-09-19. It is small, it is a fixed dated edition, it is
# published under the Open Government Licence, and canada.ca rejects scripted
# fetches often enough that a build depending on a live fetch is not
# reproducible. Git cannot re-include a path inside an excluded directory, so
# data/ is excluded file-by-file rather than wholesale.
data/*
!data/finance/
data/finance/*
!data/finance/2026/

# The temporal scope extraction is the second exception, and for a different
# reason. Everything else under data/ is a build artifact that `python -m
# portage.build` regenerates from a documented source. These are not: they are
# the output of a model, called once from a batch script, and there is no way
# to reproduce them except by calling the API again and getting different
# answers. CLAUDE.md requires that output to be committed as data. The run
# record and the batch ledger are committed with it, because a row without the
# batch, model, prompt hash and ceiling that produced it is unprovenanced.
!data/provision_temporal_scope.csv
!data/temporal_scope_rejects.csv
!data/temporal_scope_failures.csv
!data/temporal_scope_filtered.csv
!data/temporal_scope_run.json
!data/temporal_scope_batches.csv
# Hand-recorded, never written by the build: notes from the precision and
# recall checks on provisions the extraction deliberately left alone.
!data/extraction_notes.csv
# The record of what the v0.3.1 fixes moved. Not build-generated: it compares
# the current build against the released v0.3.0 database, which is a build
# artifact and is not in the repository, so nobody can regenerate this from a
# clean clone. The file is the evidence.
!data/indicator_changes_v0.3.0_to_v0.3.1.csv
*.parquet
*.xml
*.zip

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# The database is a build artifact. It gets rebuilt by `python -m portage.build`.
portage.sqlite
portage.sqlite-journal
portage.sqlite-wal
portage.sqlite-shm
build/
dist/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

